{"chunk_id": "source_buying_machinery_agreement_0", "content": "Agreement for Buying Machinery\nThis contract (“Agreement”) has been entered into December_____, 2024 (“Execution Date”)\nbetween:\n\n\n_______________ (“Buyer”) having the office situated at _____________, M.P. Nagar Zone- 1,\nBhopal, Madhya Pradesh- 462001; and\n\n\n_______________ (“Seller”) having the office situated at ________________, Nasik,\nMaharashtra (enter the pin code).\n\n\nBoth the Buyer and the Seller are hereby individually referred to as “Party” and collectively as\n“Parties”.\nIn consideration of the mutual undertakings herein contained, the Parties hereto agree as follows:\n\n\n1. Sale: The Seller agrees to sell to the Buyer and the Buyer agrees to purchase from the Seller -\n   the machines and features (“Equipment”) as listed in Schedule A to this Agreement\n   (“Schedule A”) in accordance with the terms and conditions as stipulated in the Agreement.\n\n2. Sale Price: The sale price of the Equipment is Rs. ____________ (“Price”). Out of the total\n   Price, the Buyer has already paid an advance amount of Rs. _________ on ______, 2024\n   (“Advance Amount”). The remaining sum of Price shall be paid after the Buyer obtains the\n   possession of Equipment at the place as specified hereinafter in Clause 3 of the Agreement.\n\n3. Delivery of Equipment: The Seller shall deliver the Equipment at __________ (“Place of\n   Delivery”). All shipping, installation and transit clause shall be borne by the Seller.\n\n4. Closing Date: The closing date shall take upon the delivery of the Equipment latest by\n   _____________ (“Closing Date”/ “Delivery Date”).\n\n5. Representation and Warranties:\n\n   5.1.       Both the Parties hereby represent that they are engaged in the lawful businesses\n       and have full authority to enter into this Agreement.\n\n\n                                                1\n\f   5.2.        The Seller hereby warrants that Equipment, when properly installed, operated,\n       will be free from defects in materials and workmanship for a period of ________ months\n       [insert warranty period] from the Delivery Date.\n\n   5.3.         The Seller's warranty covers the repair or replacement of defective parts. The\n       Seller's obligation is limited to the cost of repair or replacement of defective parts.\n\n   5.4.        The Seller's liability under this warranty is limited to the Price of the Equipment\n       as set forth in this Agreement.\n\n6. Title of the Equipment: Tittle to the Equipment, free and clear of all liens, claims and\n   encumbrances of any kind shall vest in the Buyer upon the payment of Price of the\n   Equipment to the Seller (as required to be paid as per the Clause 2 of this Agreement).\n\n7. Penal Interest and Damages and Termination:\n\n   7.1.        If the Seller is unable to deliver the Equipment by the Closing date or fails to\n       deliver Equipment at the Place of the Delivery by the Delivery Date, then the Seller shall\n       be liable to pay the penal interest at the rate of 20% (p.a.) of the: (a) total Price of the\n       Equipment; and (b) the Advance Amount to the Buyer, from the date of payment of\n       Advance Amount until the actual date of delivery.\n\n   7.2.        In addition to the aforesaid penal interest, the Seller shall also be liable to\n       reimburse the cost/ expenses as well as other reasonable expenses incurred by the Buyer\n       while travelling to Nasik or any other place in order to contact the Seller for making him\n       deliver the Equipment at the Place of Delivery or any other place specified by the Buyer.\n\n   7.3.      In any event, where the Seller is unable to deliver the Equipment within ________\n       months from the Execution Date, this Agreement shall terminate (“Termination”).\n\n   7.4.        Upon termination, the Seller shall return the Advance Amount along with the\n       interest rate at the rate of 20% p.a. (levied on the total Advance Amount) from the date of\n       payment of Advance Amount until the actual date of Termination of this Agreement.\n       Further, the Seller shall be liable to the pay the compensatory damages to the Buyer not\n       exceeding the total Price of the Equipment.\n\n8. Governing Law and Jurisdiction:\n\n   8.1.       This Agreement shall be governed and construed as the laws enforced in India.\n\n\n\n                                                2\n\f   8.2.       Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this purchase of the machinery\n       from the Seller shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts at\n       Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh.\n\n9. Entire Agreement: This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Seller and\n   the Buyer with respect to selling/ buying of the Equipment and supersedes all prior or\n   contemporaneous communications, representations, or agreements, whether oral or written\n   between the Parties.\n\n\nN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties have caused this Agreement to be executed and do each\nhereby warrant and represent that its signatory whose signature appears below has been and is on\nthe date of this Agreement duly authorized by all necessary and appropriate corporate action to\nexecute this Agreement.\n\n\n\n\nFor the Buyer\nTitle/ Name:____________\n(Authorized Signatory)\nSignature: _____________\nDate: ________________\n\n\nFor the Seller\nTitle/ Name:____________\n(Authorized Signatory)\nSignature: _____________\nDate: ________________\n\n\n\n\n                         (Schedule A- Description of Equipment to follow)\n\n\n                                                3\n\fSchedule A- Description of Equipment\n\n\n\n\n                 4", "contextual_content": "[source_buying_machinery_agreement.md] Agreement for Buying Machinery\nThis contract (“Agreement”) has been entered into December_____, 2024 (“Execution Date”)\nbetween:\n\n\n_______________ (“Buyer”) having the office situated at _____________, M.P. Nagar Zone- 1,\nBhopal, Madhya Pradesh- 462001; and\n\n\n_______________ (“Seller”) having the office situated at ________________, Nasik,\nMaharashtra (enter the pin code).\n\n\nBoth the Buyer and the Seller are hereby individually referred to as “Party” and collectively as\n“Parties”.\nIn consideration of the mutual undertakings herein contained, the Parties hereto agree as follows:\n\n\n1. Sale: The Seller agrees to sell to the Buyer and the Buyer agrees to purchase from the Seller -\n   the machines and features (“Equipment”) as listed in Schedule A to this Agreement\n   (“Schedule A”) in accordance with the terms and conditions as stipulated in the Agreement.\n\n2. Sale Price: The sale price of the Equipment is Rs. ____________ (“Price”). Out of the total\n   Price, the Buyer has already paid an advance amount of Rs. _________ on ______, 2024\n   (“Advance Amount”). The remaining sum of Price shall be paid after the Buyer obtains the\n   possession of Equipment at the place as specified hereinafter in Clause 3 of the Agreement.\n\n3. Delivery of Equipment: The Seller shall deliver the Equipment at __________ (“Place of\n   Delivery”). All shipping, installation and transit clause shall be borne by the Seller.\n\n4. Closing Date: The closing date shall take upon the delivery of the Equipment latest by\n   _____________ (“Closing Date”/ “Delivery Date”).\n\n5. Representation and Warranties:\n\n   5.1.       Both the Parties hereby represent that they are engaged in the lawful businesses\n       and have full authority to enter into this Agreement.\n\n\n                                                1\n\f   5.2.        The Seller hereby warrants that Equipment, when properly installed, operated,\n       will be free from defects in materials and workmanship for a period of ________ months\n       [insert warranty period] from the Delivery Date.\n\n   5.3.         The Seller's warranty covers the repair or replacement of defective parts. The\n       Seller's obligation is limited to the cost of repair or replacement of defective parts.\n\n   5.4.        The Seller's liability under this warranty is limited to the Price of the Equipment\n       as set forth in this Agreement.\n\n6. Title of the Equipment: Tittle to the Equipment, free and clear of all liens, claims and\n   encumbrances of any kind shall vest in the Buyer upon the payment of Price of the\n   Equipment to the Seller (as required to be paid as per the Clause 2 of this Agreement).\n\n7. Penal Interest and Damages and Termination:\n\n   7.1.        If the Seller is unable to deliver the Equipment by the Closing date or fails to\n       deliver Equipment at the Place of the Delivery by the Delivery Date, then the Seller shall\n       be liable to pay the penal interest at the rate of 20% (p.a.) of the: (a) total Price of the\n       Equipment; and (b) the Advance Amount to the Buyer, from the date of payment of\n       Advance Amount until the actual date of delivery.\n\n   7.2.        In addition to the aforesaid penal interest, the Seller shall also be liable to\n       reimburse the cost/ expenses as well as other reasonable expenses incurred by the Buyer\n       while travelling to Nasik or any other place in order to contact the Seller for making him\n       deliver the Equipment at the Place of Delivery or any other place specified by the Buyer.\n\n   7.3.      In any event, where the Seller is unable to deliver the Equipment within ________\n       months from the Execution Date, this Agreement shall terminate (“Termination”).\n\n   7.4.        Upon termination, the Seller shall return the Advance Amount along with the\n       interest rate at the rate of 20% p.a. (levied on the total Advance Amount) from the date of\n       payment of Advance Amount until the actual date of Termination of this Agreement.\n       Further, the Seller shall be liable to the pay the compensatory damages to the Buyer not\n       exceeding the total Price of the Equipment.\n\n8. Governing Law and Jurisdiction:\n\n   8.1.       This Agreement shall be governed and construed as the laws enforced in India.\n\n\n\n                                                2\n\f   8.2.       Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this purchase of the machinery\n       from the Seller shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts at\n       Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh.\n\n9. Entire Agreement: This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Seller and\n   the Buyer with respect to selling/ buying of the Equipment and supersedes all prior or\n   contemporaneous communications, representations, or agreements, whether oral or written\n   between the Parties.\n\n\nN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties have caused this Agreement to be executed and do each\nhereby warrant and represent that its signatory whose signature appears below has been and is on\nthe date of this Agreement duly authorized by all necessary and appropriate corporate action to\nexecute this Agreement.\n\n\n\n\nFor the Buyer\nTitle/ Name:____________\n(Authorized Signatory)\nSignature: _____________\nDate: ________________\n\n\nFor the Seller\nTitle/ Name:____________\n(Authorized Signatory)\nSignature: _____________\nDate: ________________\n\n\n\n\n                         (Schedule A- Description of Equipment to follow)\n\n\n                                                3\n\fSchedule A- Description of Equipment\n\n\n\n\n                 4", "metadata": {"doc_type": "other", "standard_body": null, "material_class": null, "export_control_regime": null, "process_type": [], "jurisdiction": ["IN"], "topic": "general"}, "embedding": [-0.00036907196044921875, 0.05877685546875, 0.031982421875, -0.01763916015625, -0.0018482208251953125, 0.0081024169921875, -0.0101165771484375, -0.0099334716796875, -0.0307159423828125, 0.03546142578125, 0.07879638671875, -0.046051025390625, -0.0421142578125, -0.029083251953125, 0.045654296875, 0.047546386718